Children Appear From Nowhere","body":"The motel pool was refilled for the season, and within an hour it held more children than the town has on record. The manager has stopped asking for room numbers.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Sunset Declared Best Of The Year By Committee","body":"The sunset committee met on the ridge on Friday and declared this year's best. Minutes record it as orange with purple, which narrows it down somewhat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"February 2131","year":2131.0,"month":2.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"quiet_month","headline":"A Quiet Month In Old Bottle","body":"By every measure the Dispatch keeps, 2131 in Old Bottle continued at its usual pace this month. No sirens, no speeches, and the dust settled where it fell.\n\nOld-timers on the courthouse bench called it the best kind of news. The editor, who has a page to fill, disagreed but was outvoted.","priority":0.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Snow Falls On Old Bottle; Nobody Owns A Shovel","body":"A rare snowfall dusted Old Bottle overnight and was gone by lunch. In the interval, residents photographed it, tasted it, and looked for a shovel that does not exist.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Annual Chili Cook-Off Won By Same Man For Ninth Year","body":"The chili cook-off was won again by the same fellow with the same recipe, which he will not share. Second place was awarded to a pot that a judge described as brave.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Windmill Squeak Finally Oiled; Town Can't Sleep Without It","body":"The windmill by the stockyard has been oiled after years of squeaking. Several residents report insomnia and have asked for it to be put back the way it was.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Ghost Town Tour Canceled After Ghost Town Gets Residents","body":"The weekly tour of the abandoned settlement up the road has been called off, as three families have moved in and object to being photographed.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Scorpion Found In Boot; Boot Found In Yard","body":"A resident discovered a scorpion in his boot on Monday morning. The boot was last seen traveling at speed across the lawn. Both are recovering.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"March 2131","year":2131.0,"month":3.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"approval_vote","headline":"Voters Weigh In; Mayor Sierra Scores 43","body":"The annual approval poll put Mayor Sierra at 43 percent this year. The top complaint, as ever, was whatever residents had waited longest for.\n\nThe mayor's office said the number speaks for itself. Everyone else said it too, meaning different things.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Tumbleweed The Size Of A Truck Rolls Through Downtown","body":"A tumbleweed of unusual size crossed downtown on Sunday, paused at a stop sign, and continued east. Witnesses agree it had the right of way.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Farmers' Market Opens; Mostly Melons, Mostly Fine","body":"The Saturday market opened for the season with a strong showing of melons and one table of jam. Attendance was high, as was the temperature.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Water Tower Repainted; Town Name Spelled Right This Time","body":"The water tower received a fresh coat of paint and, after some discussion, the correct spelling of Old Bottle. The painter blamed the wind for last time.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Gas Station Adds Ice Machine; Traffic Jam Follows","body":"The gas station at the edge of town installed an ice machine and immediately caused the largest traffic jam in Old Bottle history. Police describe the crowd as orderly and damp.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Neon Sign Repaired; Now Reads Correctly For First Time In Years","body":"The motel sign that has read MOT L since anyone can remember has been fixed. Longtime residents say it looks wrong.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"April 2131","year":2131.0,"month":4.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"10 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 10 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Mayor Sierra Cuts Ribbon; Scissors Also Cut Mayor","body":"The ribbon-cutting at the new bench went ahead with a minor injury to Mayor Sierra, who described the scissors as sharper than expected. The bench is open.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Local Man Claims To Have Seen Rain; Others Skeptical","body":"A resident reports seeing rain fall on the north end of town. Nobody else saw it, the ground was dry by the time anyone looked, and the matter has been referred to the weather office.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Painted Rock On Hill Repainted; Now Also Wrong Color","body":"The big rock on the hill was repainted overnight by persons unknown. The council has decided that this year's color is the official one until someone changes it.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Petrified Log Returned To Roadside Attraction After Forty Years","body":"A petrified log taken from the roadside attraction decades ago arrived by post with an apology. The attraction has put it back and framed the letter.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Annual Chili Cook-Off Won By Same Man For Ninth Year","body":"The chili cook-off was won again by the same fellow with the same recipe, which he will not share. Second place was awarded to a pot that a judge described as brave.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"May 2131","year":2131.0,"month":5.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 11 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Dust Storm Sandblasts Every Windshield In Town","body":"A wall of dust rolled through on Thursday and left every car in Old Bottle the same shade of tan. The car wash is booked for a month.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Tumbleweed The Size Of A Truck Rolls Through Downtown","body":"A tumbleweed of unusual size crossed downtown on Sunday, paused at a stop sign, and continued east. Witnesses agree it had the right of way.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Windmill Squeak Finally Oiled; Town Can't Sleep Without It","body":"The windmill by the stockyard has been oiled after years of squeaking. Several residents report insomnia and have asked for it to be put back the way it was.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Snow Falls On Old Bottle; Nobody Owns A Shovel","body":"A rare snowfall dusted Old Bottle overnight and was gone by lunch. In the interval, residents photographed it, tasted it, and looked for a shovel that does not exist.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Motel Pool Refilled; Children Appear From Nowhere","body":"The motel pool was refilled for the season, and within an hour it held more children than the town has on record. The manager has stopped asking for room numbers.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"June 2131","year":2131.0,"month":6.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"neighbor_news","headline":"Neighboring Goldfield Junction Reports A Busy Month","body":"Word arrived from Goldfield Junction, our neighbor down the highway, of growth and ambition over there. Their population and ours now trade back and forth across the line.\n\nRelations remain cordial. Their football team is another matter.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Windmill Squeak Finally Oiled; Town Can't Sleep Without It","body":"The windmill by the stockyard has been oiled after years of squeaking. Several residents report insomnia and have asked for it to be put back the way it was.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Annual Chili Cook-Off Won By Same Man For Ninth Year","body":"The chili cook-off was won again by the same fellow with the same recipe, which he will not share. Second place was awarded to a pot that a judge described as brave.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Mystery Hum Traced To Refrigerator At The Feed Store","body":"The low hum that has puzzled the east side for a month has been traced to a refrigerator at the feed store. It has been switched off and the mystery is over, to general disappointment.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Swap Meet Trades Same Lamp For Fifth Year Running","body":"A brass lamp changed hands again at the swap meet and is now believed to have lived in every house on the west side. Its current owner intends to keep it, which nobody believes.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Radio Station Adds Second Record","body":"The local station has acquired a second record and will alternate it with the first. Listeners are advised that the second one is a waltz.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"July 2131","year":2131.0,"month":7.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Boarded Windows Multiply Near Old Bottle","body":"Another 8 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"advisor_need","headline":"Advisors Press Council On Transport","body":"The advisors' office delivered its monthly memorandum on Transport to Mayor Sierra. It was short, underlined, and left on top of the pile.\n\nThe mayor's office confirmed receipt. Residents confirmed the problem.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Local Man Claims To Have Seen Rain; Others Skeptical","body":"A resident reports seeing rain fall on the north end of town. Nobody else saw it, the ground was dry by the time anyone looked, and the matter has been referred to the weather office.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Retired Prospector Finds Nothing, Reports Good Day","body":"A retired prospector returned from the hills with an empty sack and a broad smile. Asked what he found, he said quiet, and recommended it.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Motel Pool Refilled; Children Appear From Nowhere","body":"The motel pool was refilled for the season, and within an hour it held more children than the town has on record. The manager has stopped asking for room numbers.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Water Tower Repainted; Town Name Spelled Right This Time","body":"The water tower received a fresh coat of paint and, after some discussion, the correct spelling of Old Bottle. The painter blamed the wind for last time.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"August 2131","year":2131.0,"month":8.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"tourism_event_announced","headline":"City Sports Festival Scheduled For September 2131","body":"Old Bottle has announced City Sports Festival for September 2131. Eligible visitor markets receive a seasonal event boost, subject to available transport, staff, beds, power and water.\n\nOrganizers warned that the event will be cancelled if its qualifying services are lost before the big day. Hotel managers were already counting rooms.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 10 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Annual Chili Cook-Off Won By Same Man For Ninth Year","body":"The chili cook-off was won again by the same fellow with the same recipe, which he will not share. Second place was awarded to a pot that a judge described as brave.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Heat Wave Enters Third Week; Sidewalks Fry Eggs, Reporters Confirm","body":"Temperatures held above anything reasonable for a third week. The Dispatch tested the sidewalk-egg theory and can report that it works, if you like your eggs with grit.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Drive-In Reopens With Double Feature And Single Speaker","body":"The drive-in screened its first films in years to a full lot. The one working speaker was placed in the middle and people parked around it like a campfire.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Rodeo Weekend Leaves Town Sore But Happy","body":"Rodeo weekend came and went with the usual mix of bruises, dust and sunburn. The bull, which has a name, was declared the winner again.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"September 2131","year":2131.0,"month":9.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"neighbor_shock","headline":"Neighbor Coyote Springs Has A Very Bad Month","body":"Our neighbor Coyote Springs suffered a sudden setback this month, the details of which vary with the teller. Trade across the line has slowed while they sort themselves out.\n\nOld Bottle has offered help. Coyote Springs has offered thanks and a request for lumber.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 9 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Tumbleweed The Size Of A Truck Rolls Through Downtown","body":"A tumbleweed of unusual size crossed downtown on Sunday, paused at a stop sign, and continued east. Witnesses agree it had the right of way.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Jackrabbit Population Booms; Gardeners Despair","body":"A wet spring has produced more jackrabbits than anyone can count, and they are eating everything green within city limits. One resident has begun naming them, which is not a solution.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Giant Fiberglass Cactus Draws Visitors, Confuses Birds","body":"The roadside cactus on the highway into town is now the tallest thing for miles. Motorists stop for photographs and birds stop to be disappointed.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Neon Sign Repaired; Now Reads Correctly For First Time In Years","body":"The motel sign that has read MOT L since anyone can remember has been fixed. Longtime residents say it looks wrong.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"October 2131","year":2131.0,"month":10.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"tourism_event_announced","headline":"City Convention Scheduled For November 2131","body":"Old Bottle has announced City Convention for November 2131. Eligible visitor markets receive a seasonal event boost, subject to available transport, staff, beds, power and water.\n\nOrganizers warned that the event will be cancelled if its qualifying services are lost before the big day. Hotel managers were already counting rooms.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"11 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 11 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Old-Timers Bench Gets New Slat; Old-Timers Suspicious","body":"The bench outside the courthouse has a new slat. Its regular occupants tested it for an afternoon and concluded that it will do, for now.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Gas Station Adds Ice Machine; Traffic Jam Follows","body":"The gas station at the edge of town installed an ice machine and immediately caused the largest traffic jam in Old Bottle history. Police describe the crowd as orderly and damp.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Motel Pool Refilled; Children Appear From Nowhere","body":"The motel pool was refilled for the season, and within an hour it held more children than the town has on record. The manager has stopped asking for room numbers.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Rodeo Weekend Leaves Town Sore But Happy","body":"Rodeo weekend came and went with the usual mix of bruises, dust and sunburn. The bull, which has a name, was declared the winner again.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"November 2131","year":2131.0,"month":11.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Tumbleweeds Reclaim A Block Of Old Bottle","body":"Another 10 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Radio Station Adds Second Record","body":"The local station has acquired a second record and will alternate it with the first. Listeners are advised that the second one is a waltz.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Neon Sign Repaired; Now Reads Correctly For First Time In Years","body":"The motel sign that has read MOT L since anyone can remember has been fixed. Longtime residents say it looks wrong.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Water Tower Repainted; Town Name Spelled Right This Time","body":"The water tower received a fresh coat of paint and, after some discussion, the correct spelling of Old Bottle. The painter blamed the wind for last time.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Cactus Blooms Overnight; Town Turns Out To Look","body":"The night-blooming cactus outside the library opened at last, and half of Old Bottle stood around it in bathrobes. It closed by morning, as is its habit.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Barbershop Quartet Now A Trio; Tenor Moved To The Coast","body":"The town quartet has lost its tenor to a job on the coast. Auditions are open. Applicants are warned that the repertoire is mostly about trains.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"December 2131","year":2131.0,"month":12.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Tumbleweeds Reclaim A Block Of Old Bottle","body":"Another 10 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Lizard Races Return To The Fairgrounds","body":"The annual lizard races drew a full grandstand this year. The favorite refused to leave the starting line, which is understandable in this heat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Giant Fiberglass Cactus Draws Visitors, Confuses Birds","body":"The roadside cactus on the highway into town is now the tallest thing for miles. Motorists stop for photographs and birds stop to be disappointed.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Well-Digging Contest Ends In Draw, Mud","body":"The well-digging contest at the fair ended when both teams struck water at the same moment and then each other. No winner was declared, but everyone was clean for once.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Water Tower Repainted; Town Name Spelled Right This Time","body":"The water tower received a fresh coat of paint and, after some discussion, the correct spelling of Old Bottle. The painter blamed the wind for last time.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Hardware Store Sells Out Of Shade Cloth In One Afternoon","body":"A shipment of shade cloth lasted about four hours at the hardware store on Saturday. The owner has ordered more and a rope for the queue.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"January 2132","year":2132.0,"month":1.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Boarded Windows Multiply Near Old Bottle","body":"Another 15 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"advisor_need","headline":"Advisors Press Council On Transport","body":"The advisors' office delivered its monthly memorandum on Transport to Mayor Sierra. It was short, underlined, and left on top of the pile.\n\nThe mayor's office confirmed receipt. Residents confirmed the problem.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Gas Station Adds Ice Machine; Traffic Jam Follows","body":"The gas station at the edge of town installed an ice machine and immediately caused the largest traffic jam in Old Bottle history. Police describe the crowd as orderly and damp.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Hot Springs Reopen; Smell Described As Character","body":"The hot springs south of town reopened after repairs. Visitors are reminded that the smell is natural, historic, and part of the experience.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Jackrabbit Population Booms; Gardeners Despair","body":"A wet spring has produced more jackrabbits than anyone can count, and they are eating everything green within city limits. One resident has begun naming them, which is not a solution.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Drive-In Reopens With Double Feature And Single Speaker","body":"The drive-in screened its first films in years to a full lot. The one working speaker was placed in the middle and people parked around it like a campfire.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"February 2132","year":2132.0,"month":2.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 11 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Retired Prospector Finds Nothing, Reports Good Day","body":"A retired prospector returned from the hills with an empty sack and a broad smile. Asked what he found, he said quiet, and recommended it.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Drive-In Reopens With Double Feature And Single Speaker","body":"The drive-in screened its first films in years to a full lot. The one working speaker was placed in the middle and people parked around it like a campfire.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Jackrabbit Population Booms; Gardeners Despair","body":"A wet spring has produced more jackrabbits than anyone can count, and they are eating everything green within city limits. One resident has begun naming them, which is not a solution.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Gas Station Adds Ice Machine; Traffic Jam Follows","body":"The gas station at the edge of town installed an ice machine and immediately caused the largest traffic jam in Old Bottle history. Police describe the crowd as orderly and damp.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Motel Pool Refilled; Children Appear From Nowhere","body":"The motel pool was refilled for the season, and within an hour it held more children than the town has on record. The manager has stopped asking for room numbers.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"March 2132","year":2132.0,"month":3.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"approval_vote","headline":"Voters Weigh In; Mayor Sierra Scores 43","body":"The annual approval poll put Mayor Sierra at 43 percent this year. The top complaint, as ever, was whatever residents had waited longest for.\n\nThe mayor's office said the number speaks for itself. Everyone else said it too, meaning different things.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 8 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"High School Team Wins By Forfeit; Other Team Lost In Desert","body":"The visiting team took a wrong turn on the way to Friday's game and was found by a rancher some hours later. The home side has claimed the win and a photograph of the tumbleweed they blame.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Mayor Sierra Cuts Ribbon; Scissors Also Cut Mayor","body":"The ribbon-cutting at the new bench went ahead with a minor injury to Mayor Sierra, who described the scissors as sharper than expected. The bench is open.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Well-Digging Contest Ends In Draw, Mud","body":"The well-digging contest at the fair ended when both teams struck water at the same moment and then each other. No winner was declared, but everyone was clean for once.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Town Clock Repaired; Runs Fast Out Of Enthusiasm","body":"The courthouse clock has been repaired and now gains a minute a day. The clockmaker says it will settle down once it gets used to the heat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"April 2132","year":2132.0,"month":4.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"11 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 11 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"neighbor_news","headline":"Across The County Line, Goldfield Junction Makes Plans","body":"Word arrived from Goldfield Junction, our neighbor down the highway, of growth and ambition over there. Their population and ours now trade back and forth across the line.\n\nRelations remain cordial. Their football team is another matter.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Windmill Squeak Finally Oiled; Town Can't Sleep Without It","body":"The windmill by the stockyard has been oiled after years of squeaking. Several residents report insomnia and have asked for it to be put back the way it was.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Barbershop Quartet Now A Trio; Tenor Moved To The Coast","body":"The town quartet has lost its tenor to a job on the coast. Auditions are open. Applicants are warned that the repertoire is mostly about trains.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Swap Meet Trades Same Lamp For Fifth Year Running","body":"A brass lamp changed hands again at the swap meet and is now believed to have lived in every house on the west side. Its current owner intends to keep it, which nobody believes.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Jackrabbit Population Booms; Gardeners Despair","body":"A wet spring has produced more jackrabbits than anyone can count, and they are eating everything green within city limits. One resident has begun naming them, which is not a solution.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"May 2132","year":2132.0,"month":5.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Boarded Windows Multiply Near Old Bottle","body":"Another 12 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Town Clock Repaired; Runs Fast Out Of Enthusiasm","body":"The courthouse clock has been repaired and now gains a minute a day. The clockmaker says it will settle down once it gets used to the heat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Drive-In Reopens With Double Feature And Single Speaker","body":"The drive-in screened its first films in years to a full lot. The one working speaker was placed in the middle and people parked around it like a campfire.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Swap Meet Trades Same Lamp For Fifth Year Running","body":"A brass lamp changed hands again at the swap meet and is now believed to have lived in every house on the west side. Its current owner intends to keep it, which nobody believes.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Mineral Springs Water Now Bottled; Tastes Like Nickels","body":"A local outfit has begun bottling the mineral springs water. The label promises vitality. The taste promises pocket change.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Petrified Log Returned To Roadside Attraction After Forty Years","body":"A petrified log taken from the roadside attraction decades ago arrived by post with an apology. The attraction has put it back and framed the letter.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"June 2132","year":2132.0,"month":6.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"10 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 10 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Fishing Derby Held At Reservoir; Fish Decline To Participate","body":"The fishing derby went ahead despite the fish, who kept to the deep end. The prize for largest catch went to a hat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Stray Burro Adopted By Fire Station","body":"A burro that wandered into the fire station has been adopted by the crew. It answers to Chief and has already been photographed in a helmet.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Drive-In Reopens With Double Feature And Single Speaker","body":"The drive-in screened its first films in years to a full lot. The one working speaker was placed in the middle and people parked around it like a campfire.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Neon Sign Repaired; Now Reads Correctly For First Time In Years","body":"The motel sign that has read MOT L since anyone can remember has been fixed. Longtime residents say it looks wrong.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"High School Team Wins By Forfeit; Other Team Lost In Desert","body":"The visiting team took a wrong turn on the way to Friday's game and was found by a rancher some hours later. The home side has claimed the win and a photograph of the tumbleweed they blame.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"July 2132","year":2132.0,"month":7.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Tumbleweeds Reclaim A Block Of Old Bottle","body":"Another 14 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"advisor_need","headline":"Council Told Transport Can't Wait","body":"The advisors' office delivered its monthly memorandum on Transport to Mayor Sierra. It was short, underlined, and left on top of the pile.\n\nThe mayor's office confirmed receipt. Residents confirmed the problem.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Snow Falls On Old Bottle; Nobody Owns A Shovel","body":"A rare snowfall dusted Old Bottle overnight and was gone by lunch. In the interval, residents photographed it, tasted it, and looked for a shovel that does not exist.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Old-Timers Bench Gets New Slat; Old-Timers Suspicious","body":"The bench outside the courthouse has a new slat. Its regular occupants tested it for an afternoon and concluded that it will do, for now.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Lizard Races Return To The Fairgrounds","body":"The annual lizard races drew a full grandstand this year. The favorite refused to leave the starting line, which is understandable in this heat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Hot Springs Reopen; Smell Described As Character","body":"The hot springs south of town reopened after repairs. Visitors are reminded that the smell is natural, historic, and part of the experience.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"August 2132","year":2132.0,"month":8.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"tourism_event_announced","headline":"Old Bottle Books City Sports Festival For September 2132","body":"Old Bottle has announced City Sports Festival for September 2132. Eligible visitor markets receive a seasonal event boost, subject to available transport, staff, beds, power and water.\n\nOrganizers warned that the event will be cancelled if its qualifying services are lost before the big day. Hotel managers were already counting rooms.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 11 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Hardware Store Sells Out Of Shade Cloth In One Afternoon","body":"A shipment of shade cloth lasted about four hours at the hardware store on Saturday. The owner has ordered more and a rope for the queue.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Sunset Declared Best Of The Year By Committee","body":"The sunset committee met on the ridge on Friday and declared this year's best. Minutes record it as orange with purple, which narrows it down somewhat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Giant Fiberglass Cactus Draws Visitors, Confuses Birds","body":"The roadside cactus on the highway into town is now the tallest thing for miles. Motorists stop for photographs and birds stop to be disappointed.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Old-Timers Bench Gets New Slat; Old-Timers Suspicious","body":"The bench outside the courthouse has a new slat. Its regular occupants tested it for an afternoon and concluded that it will do, for now.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"September 2132","year":2132.0,"month":9.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"11 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 11 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Motel Pool Refilled; Children Appear From Nowhere","body":"The motel pool was refilled for the season, and within an hour it held more children than the town has on record. The manager has stopped asking for room numbers.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Old Mine Shaft Fenced Off After Goat Incident","body":"The mine shaft east of town has been fenced after a goat was retrieved from it for the third time. The goat is fine and appears to enjoy the attention.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Mineral Springs Water Now Bottled; Tastes Like Nickels","body":"A local outfit has begun bottling the mineral springs water. The label promises vitality. The taste promises pocket change.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Annual Chili Cook-Off Won By Same Man For Ninth Year","body":"The chili cook-off was won again by the same fellow with the same recipe, which he will not share. Second place was awarded to a pot that a judge described as brave.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Neon Sign Repaired; Now Reads Correctly For First Time In Years","body":"The motel sign that has read MOT L since anyone can remember has been fixed. Longtime residents say it looks wrong.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"October 2132","year":2132.0,"month":10.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"tourism_event_announced","headline":"City Convention Scheduled For November 2132","body":"Old Bottle has announced City Convention for November 2132. Eligible visitor markets receive a seasonal event boost, subject to available transport, staff, beds, power and water.\n\nOrganizers warned that the event will be cancelled if its qualifying services are lost before the big day. Hotel managers were already counting rooms.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"9 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 9 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Swap Meet Trades Same Lamp For Fifth Year Running","body":"A brass lamp changed hands again at the swap meet and is now believed to have lived in every house on the west side. Its current owner intends to keep it, which nobody believes.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Local Man Claims To Have Seen Rain; Others Skeptical","body":"A resident reports seeing rain fall on the north end of town. Nobody else saw it, the ground was dry by the time anyone looked, and the matter has been referred to the weather office.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Cactus Blooms Overnight; Town Turns Out To Look","body":"The night-blooming cactus outside the library opened at last, and half of Old Bottle stood around it in bathrobes. It closed by morning, as is its habit.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Radio Station Adds Second Record","body":"The local station has acquired a second record and will alternate it with the first. Listeners are advised that the second one is a waltz.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"November 2132","year":2132.0,"month":11.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Boarded Windows Multiply Near Old Bottle","body":"Another 8 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Casino Opens With Free Peanuts, Paid Everything Else","body":"A new casino opened on the strip with a brass band, a searchlight and a buffet that ran out by nine. Management called the evening a success. Patrons called it Tuesday.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Snow Falls On Old Bottle; Nobody Owns A Shovel","body":"A rare snowfall dusted Old Bottle overnight and was gone by lunch. In the interval, residents photographed it, tasted it, and looked for a shovel that does not exist.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Mystery Hum Traced To Refrigerator At The Feed Store","body":"The low hum that has puzzled the east side for a month has been traced to a refrigerator at the feed store. It has been switched off and the mystery is over, to general disappointment.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Windmill Squeak Finally Oiled; Town Can't Sleep Without It","body":"The windmill by the stockyard has been oiled after years of squeaking. Several residents report insomnia and have asked for it to be put back the way it was.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Scorpion Found In Boot; Boot Found In Yard","body":"A resident discovered a scorpion in his boot on Monday morning. The boot was last seen traveling at speed across the lawn. Both are recovering.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"December 2132","year":2132.0,"month":12.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"8 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 8 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Barbershop Quartet Now A Trio; Tenor Moved To The Coast","body":"The town quartet has lost its tenor to a job on the coast. Auditions are open. Applicants are warned that the repertoire is mostly about trains.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Mayor Sierra Cuts Ribbon; Scissors Also Cut Mayor","body":"The ribbon-cutting at the new bench went ahead with a minor injury to Mayor Sierra, who described the scissors as sharper than expected. The bench is open.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Sunset Declared Best Of The Year By Committee","body":"The sunset committee met on the ridge on Friday and declared this year's best. Minutes record it as orange with purple, which narrows it down somewhat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Water Tower Repainted; Town Name Spelled Right This Time","body":"The water tower received a fresh coat of paint and, after some discussion, the correct spelling of Old Bottle. The painter blamed the wind for last time.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Casino Opens With Free Peanuts, Paid Everything Else","body":"A new casino opened on the strip with a brass band, a searchlight and a buffet that ran out by nine. Management called the evening a success. Patrons called it Tuesday.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"January 2133","year":2133.0,"month":1.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"8 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 8 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"advisor_need","headline":"Advisors Press Council On Transport","body":"The advisors' office delivered its monthly memorandum on Transport to Mayor Sierra. It was short, underlined, and left on top of the pile.\n\nThe mayor's office confirmed receipt. Residents confirmed the problem.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Coyotes Serenade East Side For Third Straight Night","body":"Residents of the east side report three nights of coyote song. Opinions are divided on the harmonies but not on the volume.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Swap Meet Trades Same Lamp For Fifth Year Running","body":"A brass lamp changed hands again at the swap meet and is now believed to have lived in every house on the west side. Its current owner intends to keep it, which nobody believes.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"High School Team Wins By Forfeit; Other Team Lost In Desert","body":"The visiting team took a wrong turn on the way to Friday's game and was found by a rancher some hours later. The home side has claimed the win and a photograph of the tumbleweed they blame.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Giant Fiberglass Cactus Draws Visitors, Confuses Birds","body":"The roadside cactus on the highway into town is now the tallest thing for miles. Motorists stop for photographs and birds stop to be disappointed.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"February 2133","year":2133.0,"month":2.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"9 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 9 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Sunset Declared Best Of The Year By Committee","body":"The sunset committee met on the ridge on Friday and declared this year's best. Minutes record it as orange with purple, which narrows it down somewhat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Radio Station Adds Second Record","body":"The local station has acquired a second record and will alternate it with the first. Listeners are advised that the second one is a waltz.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Dust Storm Sandblasts Every Windshield In Town","body":"A wall of dust rolled through on Thursday and left every car in Old Bottle the same shade of tan. The car wash is booked for a month.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Tumbleweed The Size Of A Truck Rolls Through Downtown","body":"A tumbleweed of unusual size crossed downtown on Sunday, paused at a stop sign, and continued east. Witnesses agree it had the right of way.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Diner Adds Second Fan; Customers Weep With Gratitude","body":"The diner on Main Street has installed a second ceiling fan. Regulars describe the difference as life-changing. The pie is unchanged.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"March 2133","year":2133.0,"month":3.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"approval_vote","headline":"Town Hall Straw Poll Delivers A Verdict","body":"The annual approval poll put Mayor Sierra at 42 percent this year. The top complaint, as ever, was whatever residents had waited longest for.\n\nThe mayor's office said the number speaks for itself. Everyone else said it too, meaning different things.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"13 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 13 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Giant Fiberglass Cactus Draws Visitors, Confuses Birds","body":"The roadside cactus on the highway into town is now the tallest thing for miles. Motorists stop for photographs and birds stop to be disappointed.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Dust Storm Sandblasts Every Windshield In Town","body":"A wall of dust rolled through on Thursday and left every car in Old Bottle the same shade of tan. The car wash is booked for a month.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Old Mine Shaft Fenced Off After Goat Incident","body":"The mine shaft east of town has been fenced after a goat was retrieved from it for the third time. The goat is fine and appears to enjoy the attention.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Tumbleweed The Size Of A Truck Rolls Through Downtown","body":"A tumbleweed of unusual size crossed downtown on Sunday, paused at a stop sign, and continued east. Witnesses agree it had the right of way.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"April 2133","year":2133.0,"month":4.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"neighbor_shock","headline":"Word From Goldfield Junction Is Not Good","body":"Our neighbor Goldfield Junction suffered a sudden setback this month, the details of which vary with the teller. Trade across the line has slowed while they sort themselves out.\n\nOld Bottle has offered help. Goldfield Junction has offered thanks and a request for lumber.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Boarded Windows Multiply Near Old Bottle","body":"Another 11 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Scorpion Found In Boot; Boot Found In Yard","body":"A resident discovered a scorpion in his boot on Monday morning. The boot was last seen traveling at speed across the lawn. Both are recovering.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Diner Adds Second Fan; Customers Weep With Gratitude","body":"The diner on Main Street has installed a second ceiling fan. Regulars describe the difference as life-changing. The pie is unchanged.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Lizard Races Return To The Fairgrounds","body":"The annual lizard races drew a full grandstand this year. The favorite refused to leave the starting line, which is understandable in this heat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Fishing Derby Held At Reservoir; Fish Decline To Participate","body":"The fishing derby went ahead despite the fish, who kept to the deep end. The prize for largest catch went to a hat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"May 2133","year":2133.0,"month":5.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Tumbleweeds Reclaim A Block Of Old Bottle","body":"Another 10 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"neighbor_news","headline":"Ironwood Flats Sends Regards And A Trade Proposal","body":"Word arrived from Ironwood Flats, our neighbor down the highway, of growth and ambition over there. Their population and ours now trade back and forth across the line.\n\nRelations remain cordial. Their football team is another matter.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Casino Opens With Free Peanuts, Paid Everything Else","body":"A new casino opened on the strip with a brass band, a searchlight and a buffet that ran out by nine. Management called the evening a success. Patrons called it Tuesday.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Stray Burro Adopted By Fire Station","body":"A burro that wandered into the fire station has been adopted by the crew. It answers to Chief and has already been photographed in a helmet.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Mayor Sierra Cuts Ribbon; Scissors Also Cut Mayor","body":"The ribbon-cutting at the new bench went ahead with a minor injury to Mayor Sierra, who described the scissors as sharper than expected. The bench is open.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Windmill Squeak Finally Oiled; Town Can't Sleep Without It","body":"The windmill by the stockyard has been oiled after years of squeaking. Several residents report insomnia and have asked for it to be put back the way it was.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"June 2133","year":2133.0,"month":6.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"14 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 14 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Tumbleweed The Size Of A Truck Rolls Through Downtown","body":"A tumbleweed of unusual size crossed downtown on Sunday, paused at a stop sign, and continued east. Witnesses agree it had the right of way.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Casino Opens With Free Peanuts, Paid Everything Else","body":"A new casino opened on the strip with a brass band, a searchlight and a buffet that ran out by nine. Management called the evening a success. Patrons called it Tuesday.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Giant Fiberglass Cactus Draws Visitors, Confuses Birds","body":"The roadside cactus on the highway into town is now the tallest thing for miles. Motorists stop for photographs and birds stop to be disappointed.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Diner Adds Second Fan; Customers Weep With Gratitude","body":"The diner on Main Street has installed a second ceiling fan. Regulars describe the difference as life-changing. The pie is unchanged.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Fishing Derby Held At Reservoir; Fish Decline To Participate","body":"The fishing derby went ahead despite the fish, who kept to the deep end. The prize for largest catch went to a hat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"July 2133","year":2133.0,"month":7.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Tumbleweeds Reclaim A Block Of Old Bottle","body":"Another 16 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"advisor_need","headline":"Advisors Press Council On Transport","body":"The advisors' office delivered its monthly memorandum on Transport to Mayor Sierra. It was short, underlined, and left on top of the pile.\n\nThe mayor's office confirmed receipt. Residents confirmed the problem.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Cactus Blooms Overnight; Town Turns Out To Look","body":"The night-blooming cactus outside the library opened at last, and half of Old Bottle stood around it in bathrobes. It closed by morning, as is its habit.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Neon Sign Repaired; Now Reads Correctly For First Time In Years","body":"The motel sign that has read MOT L since anyone can remember has been fixed. Longtime residents say it looks wrong.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Stray Burro Adopted By Fire Station","body":"A burro that wandered into the fire station has been adopted by the crew. It answers to Chief and has already been photographed in a helmet.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Painted Rock On Hill Repainted; Now Also Wrong Color","body":"The big rock on the hill was repainted overnight by persons unknown. The council has decided that this year's color is the official one until someone changes it.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"August 2133","year":2133.0,"month":8.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"tourism_event_announced","headline":"Mark The Calendar: City Sports Festival Comes In September 2133","body":"Old Bottle has announced City Sports Festival for September 2133. Eligible visitor markets receive a seasonal event boost, subject to available transport, staff, beds, power and water.\n\nOrganizers warned that the event will be cancelled if its qualifying services are lost before the big day. Hotel managers were already counting rooms.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Tumbleweeds Reclaim A Block Of Old Bottle","body":"Another 17 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"neighbor_news","headline":"Coyote Springs Sends Regards And A Trade Proposal","body":"Word arrived from Coyote Springs, our neighbor down the highway, of growth and ambition over there. Their population and ours now trade back and forth across the line.\n\nRelations remain cordial. Their football team is another matter.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Rodeo Weekend Leaves Town Sore But Happy","body":"Rodeo weekend came and went with the usual mix of bruises, dust and sunburn. The bull, which has a name, was declared the winner again.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Chili Cook-Off Judge Recovers; Vows To Return","body":"The judge hospitalized after last month's cook-off has recovered and says he will be back next year. His doctor has other views.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Gas Station Adds Ice Machine; Traffic Jam Follows","body":"The gas station at the edge of town installed an ice machine and immediately caused the largest traffic jam in Old Bottle history. Police describe the crowd as orderly and damp.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"September 2133","year":2133.0,"month":9.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 18 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"neighbor_news","headline":"News From Down The Road: Ironwood Flats Grows","body":"Word arrived from Ironwood Flats, our neighbor down the highway, of growth and ambition over there. Their population and ours now trade back and forth across the line.\n\nRelations remain cordial. Their football team is another matter.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Farmers' Market Opens; Mostly Melons, Mostly Fine","body":"The Saturday market opened for the season with a strong showing of melons and one table of jam. Attendance was high, as was the temperature.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Drive-In Reopens With Double Feature And Single Speaker","body":"The drive-in screened its first films in years to a full lot. The one working speaker was placed in the middle and people parked around it like a campfire.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Diner Adds Second Fan; Customers Weep With Gratitude","body":"The diner on Main Street has installed a second ceiling fan. Regulars describe the difference as life-changing. The pie is unchanged.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Annual Chili Cook-Off Won By Same Man For Ninth Year","body":"The chili cook-off was won again by the same fellow with the same recipe, which he will not share. Second place was awarded to a pot that a judge described as brave.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"October 2133","year":2133.0,"month":10.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"economy_shift","headline":"Outlook Shifts To Slow Growth For The Region","body":"The national outlook has shifted to Slow Growth, according to the people paid to say such things. Local factories and shops will feel it over the coming months.\n\nThe chamber of commerce urged calm, then quietly checked its savings.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"tourism_event_announced","headline":"Old Bottle Books City Convention For November 2133","body":"Old Bottle has announced City Convention for November 2133. Eligible visitor markets receive a seasonal event boost, subject to available transport, staff, beds, power and water.\n\nOrganizers warned that the event will be cancelled if its qualifying services are lost before the big day. Hotel managers were already counting rooms.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 10 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Mineral Springs Water Now Bottled; Tastes Like Nickels","body":"A local outfit has begun bottling the mineral springs water. The label promises vitality. The taste promises pocket change.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Swap Meet Trades Same Lamp For Fifth Year Running","body":"A brass lamp changed hands again at the swap meet and is now believed to have lived in every house on the west side. Its current owner intends to keep it, which nobody believes.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Motel Pool Refilled; Children Appear From Nowhere","body":"The motel pool was refilled for the season, and within an hour it held more children than the town has on record. The manager has stopped asking for room numbers.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"November 2133","year":2133.0,"month":11.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 10 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Casino Opens With Free Peanuts, Paid Everything Else","body":"A new casino opened on the strip with a brass band, a searchlight and a buffet that ran out by nine. Management called the evening a success. Patrons called it Tuesday.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Scorpion Found In Boot; Boot Found In Yard","body":"A resident discovered a scorpion in his boot on Monday morning. The boot was last seen traveling at speed across the lawn. Both are recovering.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Stray Burro Adopted By Fire Station","body":"A burro that wandered into the fire station has been adopted by the crew. It answers to Chief and has already been photographed in a helmet.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Bingo Night Moved To Larger Hall After Standing-Room Crowd","body":"Wednesday bingo has outgrown the church basement and will move to the grange hall. The caller has been given a microphone and a warning about volume.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Tumbleweed The Size Of A Truck Rolls Through Downtown","body":"A tumbleweed of unusual size crossed downtown on Sunday, paused at a stop sign, and continued east. Witnesses agree it had the right of way.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"December 2133","year":2133.0,"month":12.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"16 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 16 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Barbershop Quartet Now A Trio; Tenor Moved To The Coast","body":"The town quartet has lost its tenor to a job on the coast. Auditions are open. Applicants are warned that the repertoire is mostly about trains.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Old-Timers Bench Gets New Slat; Old-Timers Suspicious","body":"The bench outside the courthouse has a new slat. Its regular occupants tested it for an afternoon and concluded that it will do, for now.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Stray Burro Adopted By Fire Station","body":"A burro that wandered into the fire station has been adopted by the crew. It answers to Chief and has already been photographed in a helmet.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Annual Chili Cook-Off Won By Same Man For Ninth Year","body":"The chili cook-off was won again by the same fellow with the same recipe, which he will not share. Second place was awarded to a pot that a judge described as brave.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Snow Falls On Old Bottle; Nobody Owns A Shovel","body":"A rare snowfall dusted Old Bottle overnight and was gone by lunch. In the interval, residents photographed it, tasted it, and looked for a shovel that does not exist.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"January 2134","year":2134.0,"month":1.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 18 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"advisor_need","headline":"Transport: The Word From The Advisors' Office","body":"The advisors' office delivered its monthly memorandum on Transport to Mayor Sierra. It was short, underlined, and left on top of the pile.\n\nThe mayor's office confirmed receipt. Residents confirmed the problem.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Motel Pool Refilled; Children Appear From Nowhere","body":"The motel pool was refilled for the season, and within an hour it held more children than the town has on record. The manager has stopped asking for room numbers.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Hardware Store Sells Out Of Shade Cloth In One Afternoon","body":"A shipment of shade cloth lasted about four hours at the hardware store on Saturday. The owner has ordered more and a rope for the queue.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Drive-In Reopens With Double Feature And Single Speaker","body":"The drive-in screened its first films in years to a full lot. The one working speaker was placed in the middle and people parked around it like a campfire.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Old Mine Shaft Fenced Off After Goat Incident","body":"The mine shaft east of town has been fenced after a goat was retrieved from it for the third time. The goat is fine and appears to enjoy the attention.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"February 2134","year":2134.0,"month":2.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 10 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Radio Station Adds Second Record","body":"The local station has acquired a second record and will alternate it with the first. Listeners are advised that the second one is a waltz.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Windmill Squeak Finally Oiled; Town Can't Sleep Without It","body":"The windmill by the stockyard has been oiled after years of squeaking. Several residents report insomnia and have asked for it to be put back the way it was.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Petrified Log Returned To Roadside Attraction After Forty Years","body":"A petrified log taken from the roadside attraction decades ago arrived by post with an apology. The attraction has put it back and framed the letter.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Lizard Races Return To The Fairgrounds","body":"The annual lizard races drew a full grandstand this year. The favorite refused to leave the starting line, which is understandable in this heat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Motel Pool Refilled; Children Appear From Nowhere","body":"The motel pool was refilled for the season, and within an hour it held more children than the town has on record. The manager has stopped asking for room numbers.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"March 2134","year":2134.0,"month":3.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"approval_vote","headline":"Voters Weigh In; Mayor Sierra Scores 52","body":"The annual approval poll put Mayor Sierra at 52 percent this year. The top complaint, as ever, was whatever residents had waited longest for.\n\nThe mayor's office said the number speaks for itself. Everyone else said it too, meaning different things.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 8 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Lizard Races Return To The Fairgrounds","body":"The annual lizard races drew a full grandstand this year. The favorite refused to leave the starting line, which is understandable in this heat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Gas Station Adds Ice Machine; Traffic Jam Follows","body":"The gas station at the edge of town installed an ice machine and immediately caused the largest traffic jam in Old Bottle history. Police describe the crowd as orderly and damp.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Petrified Log Returned To Roadside Attraction After Forty Years","body":"A petrified log taken from the roadside attraction decades ago arrived by post with an apology. The attraction has put it back and framed the letter.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Mineral Springs Water Now Bottled; Tastes Like Nickels","body":"A local outfit has begun bottling the mineral springs water. The label promises vitality. The taste promises pocket change.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"April 2134","year":2134.0,"month":4.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"13 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 13 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Retired Prospector Finds Nothing, Reports Good Day","body":"A retired prospector returned from the hills with an empty sack and a broad smile. Asked what he found, he said quiet, and recommended it.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Mystery Hum Traced To Refrigerator At The Feed Store","body":"The low hum that has puzzled the east side for a month has been traced to a refrigerator at the feed store. It has been switched off and the mystery is over, to general disappointment.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Neon Sign Repaired; Now Reads Correctly For First Time In Years","body":"The motel sign that has read MOT L since anyone can remember has been fixed. Longtime residents say it looks wrong.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Gas Station Adds Ice Machine; Traffic Jam Follows","body":"The gas station at the edge of town installed an ice machine and immediately caused the largest traffic jam in Old Bottle history. Police describe the crowd as orderly and damp.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Hardware Store Sells Out Of Shade Cloth In One Afternoon","body":"A shipment of shade cloth lasted about four hours at the hardware store on Saturday. The owner has ordered more and a rope for the queue.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"May 2134","year":2134.0,"month":5.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Boarded Windows Multiply Near Old Bottle","body":"Another 21 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Tumbleweed The Size Of A Truck Rolls Through Downtown","body":"A tumbleweed of unusual size crossed downtown on Sunday, paused at a stop sign, and continued east. Witnesses agree it had the right of way.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Fishing Derby Held At Reservoir; Fish Decline To Participate","body":"The fishing derby went ahead despite the fish, who kept to the deep end. The prize for largest catch went to a hat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Snow Falls On Old Bottle; Nobody Owns A Shovel","body":"A rare snowfall dusted Old Bottle overnight and was gone by lunch. In the interval, residents photographed it, tasted it, and looked for a shovel that does not exist.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Motel Pool Refilled; Children Appear From Nowhere","body":"The motel pool was refilled for the season, and within an hour it held more children than the town has on record. The manager has stopped asking for room numbers.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Chili Cook-Off Judge Recovers; Vows To Return","body":"The judge hospitalized after last month's cook-off has recovered and says he will be back next year. His doctor has other views.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"June 2134","year":2134.0,"month":6.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Boarded Windows Multiply Near Old Bottle","body":"Another 17 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Retired Prospector Finds Nothing, Reports Good Day","body":"A retired prospector returned from the hills with an empty sack and a broad smile. Asked what he found, he said quiet, and recommended it.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Swap Meet Trades Same Lamp For Fifth Year Running","body":"A brass lamp changed hands again at the swap meet and is now believed to have lived in every house on the west side. Its current owner intends to keep it, which nobody believes.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Gas Station Adds Ice Machine; Traffic Jam Follows","body":"The gas station at the edge of town installed an ice machine and immediately caused the largest traffic jam in Old Bottle history. Police describe the crowd as orderly and damp.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Well-Digging Contest Ends In Draw, Mud","body":"The well-digging contest at the fair ended when both teams struck water at the same moment and then each other. No winner was declared, but everyone was clean for once.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Water Tower Repainted; Town Name Spelled Right This Time","body":"The water tower received a fresh coat of paint and, after some discussion, the correct spelling of Old Bottle. The painter blamed the wind for last time.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"July 2134","year":2134.0,"month":7.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Tumbleweeds Reclaim A Block Of Old Bottle","body":"Another 13 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"advisor_need","headline":"Advisors Press Council On Transport","body":"The advisors' office delivered its monthly memorandum on Transport to Mayor Sierra. It was short, underlined, and left on top of the pile.\n\nThe mayor's office confirmed receipt. Residents confirmed the problem.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Swap Meet Trades Same Lamp For Fifth Year Running","body":"A brass lamp changed hands again at the swap meet and is now believed to have lived in every house on the west side. Its current owner intends to keep it, which nobody believes.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Well-Digging Contest Ends In Draw, Mud","body":"The well-digging contest at the fair ended when both teams struck water at the same moment and then each other. No winner was declared, but everyone was clean for once.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Barbershop Quartet Now A Trio; Tenor Moved To The Coast","body":"The town quartet has lost its tenor to a job on the coast. Auditions are open. Applicants are warned that the repertoire is mostly about trains.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Fishing Derby Held At Reservoir; Fish Decline To Participate","body":"The fishing derby went ahead despite the fish, who kept to the deep end. The prize for largest catch went to a hat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"August 2134","year":2134.0,"month":8.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"tourism_event_announced","headline":"City Sports Festival Scheduled For September 2134","body":"Old Bottle has announced City Sports Festival for September 2134. Eligible visitor markets receive a seasonal event boost, subject to available transport, staff, beds, power and water.\n\nOrganizers warned that the event will be cancelled if its qualifying services are lost before the big day. Hotel managers were already counting rooms.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 11 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Snow Falls On Old Bottle; Nobody Owns A Shovel","body":"A rare snowfall dusted Old Bottle overnight and was gone by lunch. In the interval, residents photographed it, tasted it, and looked for a shovel that does not exist.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Drive-In Reopens With Double Feature And Single Speaker","body":"The drive-in screened its first films in years to a full lot. The one working speaker was placed in the middle and people parked around it like a campfire.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Barbershop Quartet Now A Trio; Tenor Moved To The Coast","body":"The town quartet has lost its tenor to a job on the coast. Auditions are open. Applicants are warned that the repertoire is mostly about trains.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Painted Rock On Hill Repainted; Now Also Wrong Color","body":"The big rock on the hill was repainted overnight by persons unknown. The council has decided that this year's color is the official one until someone changes it.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"September 2134","year":2134.0,"month":9.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"13 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 13 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Giant Fiberglass Cactus Draws Visitors, Confuses Birds","body":"The roadside cactus on the highway into town is now the tallest thing for miles. Motorists stop for photographs and birds stop to be disappointed.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Annual Chili Cook-Off Won By Same Man For Ninth Year","body":"The chili cook-off was won again by the same fellow with the same recipe, which he will not share. Second place was awarded to a pot that a judge described as brave.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Radio Station Adds Second Record","body":"The local station has acquired a second record and will alternate it with the first. Listeners are advised that the second one is a waltz.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Painted Rock On Hill Repainted; Now Also Wrong Color","body":"The big rock on the hill was repainted overnight by persons unknown. The council has decided that this year's color is the official one until someone changes it.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Diner Adds Second Fan; Customers Weep With Gratitude","body":"The diner on Main Street has installed a second ceiling fan. Regulars describe the difference as life-changing. The pie is unchanged.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"October 2134","year":2134.0,"month":10.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"tourism_event_announced","headline":"Old Bottle Books City Convention For November 2134","body":"Old Bottle has announced City Convention for November 2134. Eligible visitor markets receive a seasonal event boost, subject to available transport, staff, beds, power and water.\n\nOrganizers warned that the event will be cancelled if its qualifying services are lost before the big day. Hotel managers were already counting rooms.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"11 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 11 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"neighbor_growth","headline":"Coyote Springs Passes 1,000,000 Residents","body":"Our neighbor Coyote Springs now counts more than 1,000,000 residents, and some of them work here. The highway between the towns is busier every month.\n\nThe Dispatch congratulates Coyote Springs and reminds it who was here first.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Painted Rock On Hill Repainted; Now Also Wrong Color","body":"The big rock on the hill was repainted overnight by persons unknown. The council has decided that this year's color is the official one until someone changes it.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Radio Station Adds Second Record","body":"The local station has acquired a second record and will alternate it with the first. Listeners are advised that the second one is a waltz.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Local Man Claims To Have Seen Rain; Others Skeptical","body":"A resident reports seeing rain fall on the north end of town. Nobody else saw it, the ground was dry by the time anyone looked, and the matter has been referred to the weather office.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"November 2134","year":2134.0,"month":11.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"15 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 15 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Hot Springs Reopen; Smell Described As Character","body":"The hot springs south of town reopened after repairs. Visitors are reminded that the smell is natural, historic, and part of the experience.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Dust Storm Sandblasts Every Windshield In Town","body":"A wall of dust rolled through on Thursday and left every car in Old Bottle the same shade of tan. The car wash is booked for a month.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Windmill Squeak Finally Oiled; Town Can't Sleep Without It","body":"The windmill by the stockyard has been oiled after years of squeaking. Several residents report insomnia and have asked for it to be put back the way it was.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Snow Falls On Old Bottle; Nobody Owns A Shovel","body":"A rare snowfall dusted Old Bottle overnight and was gone by lunch. In the interval, residents photographed it, tasted it, and looked for a shovel that does not exist.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Neon Sign Repaired; Now Reads Correctly For First Time In Years","body":"The motel sign that has read MOT L since anyone can remember has been fixed. Longtime residents say it looks wrong.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"December 2134","year":2134.0,"month":12.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Tumbleweeds Reclaim A Block Of Old Bottle","body":"Another 21 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Dust Storm Sandblasts Every Windshield In Town","body":"A wall of dust rolled through on Thursday and left every car in Old Bottle the same shade of tan. The car wash is booked for a month.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Heat Wave Enters Third Week; Sidewalks Fry Eggs, Reporters Confirm","body":"Temperatures held above anything reasonable for a third week. The Dispatch tested the sidewalk-egg theory and can report that it works, if you like your eggs with grit.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Old Mine Shaft Fenced Off After Goat Incident","body":"The mine shaft east of town has been fenced after a goat was retrieved from it for the third time. The goat is fine and appears to enjoy the attention.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Stray Burro Adopted By Fire Station","body":"A burro that wandered into the fire station has been adopted by the crew. It answers to Chief and has already been photographed in a helmet.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Radio Station Adds Second Record","body":"The local station has acquired a second record and will alternate it with the first. Listeners are advised that the second one is a waltz.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"January 2135","year":2135.0,"month":1.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"11 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 11 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"advisor_need","headline":"Advisors Press Council On Transport","body":"The advisors' office delivered its monthly memorandum on Transport to Mayor Sierra. It was short, underlined, and left on top of the pile.\n\nThe mayor's office confirmed receipt. Residents confirmed the problem.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Ghost Town Tour Canceled After Ghost Town Gets Residents","body":"The weekly tour of the abandoned settlement up the road has been called off, as three families have moved in and object to being photographed.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Neon Sign Repaired; Now Reads Correctly For First Time In Years","body":"The motel sign that has read MOT L since anyone can remember has been fixed. Longtime residents say it looks wrong.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Old-Timers Bench Gets New Slat; Old-Timers Suspicious","body":"The bench outside the courthouse has a new slat. Its regular occupants tested it for an afternoon and concluded that it will do, for now.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Retired Prospector Finds Nothing, Reports Good Day","body":"A retired prospector returned from the hills with an empty sack and a broad smile. Asked what he found, he said quiet, and recommended it.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"February 2135","year":2135.0,"month":2.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"14 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 14 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"neighbor_growth","headline":"Ironwood Flats Passes 500,000 Residents","body":"Our neighbor Ironwood Flats now counts more than 500,000 residents, and some of them work here. The highway between the towns is busier every month.\n\nThe Dispatch congratulates Ironwood Flats and reminds it who was here first.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Barbershop Quartet Now A Trio; Tenor Moved To The Coast","body":"The town quartet has lost its tenor to a job on the coast. Auditions are open. Applicants are warned that the repertoire is mostly about trains.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Scorpion Found In Boot; Boot Found In Yard","body":"A resident discovered a scorpion in his boot on Monday morning. The boot was last seen traveling at speed across the lawn. Both are recovering.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Well-Digging Contest Ends In Draw, Mud","body":"The well-digging contest at the fair ended when both teams struck water at the same moment and then each other. No winner was declared, but everyone was clean for once.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Stray Burro Adopted By Fire Station","body":"A burro that wandered into the fire station has been adopted by the crew. It answers to Chief and has already been photographed in a helmet.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"March 2135","year":2135.0,"month":3.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"city_milestone","headline":"Old Bottle Earns The Right To A Military Base","body":"With Old Bottle past 25,000 residents, the council may now build a Military Base. Citizens consider it earned; the treasurer considers it expensive.\n\nA site has not been chosen. Several residents have opinions about their own street.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"approval_vote","headline":"Approval Stands At 53 Percent After March Count","body":"The annual approval poll put Mayor Sierra at 53 percent this year. The top complaint, as ever, was whatever residents had waited longest for.\n\nThe mayor's office said the number speaks for itself. Everyone else said it too, meaning different things.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Tumbleweeds Reclaim A Block Of Old Bottle","body":"Another 20 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Bingo Night Moved To Larger Hall After Standing-Room Crowd","body":"Wednesday bingo has outgrown the church basement and will move to the grange hall. The caller has been given a microphone and a warning about volume.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Ghost Town Tour Canceled After Ghost Town Gets Residents","body":"The weekly tour of the abandoned settlement up the road has been called off, as three families have moved in and object to being photographed.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Mineral Springs Water Now Bottled; Tastes Like Nickels","body":"A local outfit has begun bottling the mineral springs water. The label promises vitality. The taste promises pocket change.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"April 2135","year":2135.0,"month":4.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"16 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 16 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"military_base","headline":"Old Bottle Turns Down Military Base","body":"The council declined an offer to host a military base in Old Bottle this month. The land stays open for whatever the city decides to build there.\n\nOfficials said the offer will not be repeated.","priority":150.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Jackrabbit Population Booms; Gardeners Despair","body":"A wet spring has produced more jackrabbits than anyone can count, and they are eating everything green within city limits. One resident has begun naming them, which is not a solution.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Old Mine Shaft Fenced Off After Goat Incident","body":"The mine shaft east of town has been fenced after a goat was retrieved from it for the third time. The goat is fine and appears to enjoy the attention.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Ghost Town Tour Canceled After Ghost Town Gets Residents","body":"The weekly tour of the abandoned settlement up the road has been called off, as three families have moved in and object to being photographed.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Mineral Springs Water Now Bottled; Tastes Like Nickels","body":"A local outfit has begun bottling the mineral springs water. The label promises vitality. The taste promises pocket change.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"May 2135","year":2135.0,"month":5.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Tumbleweeds Reclaim A Block Of Old Bottle","body":"Another 12 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Ghost Town Tour Canceled After Ghost Town Gets Residents","body":"The weekly tour of the abandoned settlement up the road has been called off, as three families have moved in and object to being photographed.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Windmill Squeak Finally Oiled; Town Can't Sleep Without It","body":"The windmill by the stockyard has been oiled after years of squeaking. Several residents report insomnia and have asked for it to be put back the way it was.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Casino Opens With Free Peanuts, Paid Everything Else","body":"A new casino opened on the strip with a brass band, a searchlight and a buffet that ran out by nine. Management called the evening a success. Patrons called it Tuesday.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Painted Rock On Hill Repainted; Now Also Wrong Color","body":"The big rock on the hill was repainted overnight by persons unknown. The council has decided that this year's color is the official one until someone changes it.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Neon Sign Repaired; Now Reads Correctly For First Time In Years","body":"The motel sign that has read MOT L since anyone can remember has been fixed. Longtime residents say it looks wrong.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"June 2135","year":2135.0,"month":6.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"13 Buildings Stand Empty As Tenants Move On","body":"Another 13 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Radio Station Adds Second Record","body":"The local station has acquired a second record and will alternate it with the first. Listeners are advised that the second one is a waltz.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Ghost Town Tour Canceled After Ghost Town Gets Residents","body":"The weekly tour of the abandoned settlement up the road has been called off, as three families have moved in and object to being photographed.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Petrified Log Returned To Roadside Attraction After Forty Years","body":"A petrified log taken from the roadside attraction decades ago arrived by post with an apology. The attraction has put it back and framed the letter.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Barbershop Quartet Now A Trio; Tenor Moved To The Coast","body":"The town quartet has lost its tenor to a job on the coast. Auditions are open. Applicants are warned that the repertoire is mostly about trains.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"High School Team Wins By Forfeit; Other Team Lost In Desert","body":"The visiting team took a wrong turn on the way to Friday's game and was found by a rancher some hours later. The home side has claimed the win and a photograph of the tumbleweed they blame.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"July 2135","year":2135.0,"month":7.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"advisor_need","headline":"Advisors Press Council On Transport","body":"The advisors' office delivered its monthly memorandum on Transport to Mayor Sierra. It was short, underlined, and left on top of the pile.\n\nThe mayor's office confirmed receipt. Residents confirmed the problem.","priority":200.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Mayor Sierra Cuts Ribbon; Scissors Also Cut Mayor","body":"The ribbon-cutting at the new bench went ahead with a minor injury to Mayor Sierra, who described the scissors as sharper than expected. The bench is open.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Hot Springs Reopen; Smell Described As Character","body":"The hot springs south of town reopened after repairs. Visitors are reminded that the smell is natural, historic, and part of the experience.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Windmill Squeak Finally Oiled; Town Can't Sleep Without It","body":"The windmill by the stockyard has been oiled after years of squeaking. Several residents report insomnia and have asked for it to be put back the way it was.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Gas Station Adds Ice Machine; Traffic Jam Follows","body":"The gas station at the edge of town installed an ice machine and immediately caused the largest traffic jam in Old Bottle history. Police describe the crowd as orderly and damp.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"High School Team Wins By Forfeit; Other Team Lost In Desert","body":"The visiting team took a wrong turn on the way to Friday's game and was found by a rancher some hours later. The home side has claimed the win and a photograph of the tumbleweed they blame.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"August 2135","year":2135.0,"month":8.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"tourism_event_announced","headline":"Mark The Calendar: City Sports Festival Comes In September 2135","body":"Old Bottle has announced City Sports Festival for September 2135. Eligible visitor markets receive a seasonal event boost, subject to available transport, staff, beds, power and water.\n\nOrganizers warned that the event will be cancelled if its qualifying services are lost before the big day. Hotel managers were already counting rooms.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 18 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Snow Falls On Old Bottle; Nobody Owns A Shovel","body":"A rare snowfall dusted Old Bottle overnight and was gone by lunch. In the interval, residents photographed it, tasted it, and looked for a shovel that does not exist.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Petrified Log Returned To Roadside Attraction After Forty Years","body":"A petrified log taken from the roadside attraction decades ago arrived by post with an apology. The attraction has put it back and framed the letter.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Diner Adds Second Fan; Customers Weep With Gratitude","body":"The diner on Main Street has installed a second ceiling fan. Regulars describe the difference as life-changing. The pie is unchanged.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Coyotes Serenade East Side For Third Straight Night","body":"Residents of the east side report three nights of coyote song. Opinions are divided on the harmonies but not on the volume.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"September 2135","year":2135.0,"month":9.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 10 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Rodeo Weekend Leaves Town Sore But Happy","body":"Rodeo weekend came and went with the usual mix of bruises, dust and sunburn. The bull, which has a name, was declared the winner again.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Local Man Claims To Have Seen Rain; Others Skeptical","body":"A resident reports seeing rain fall on the north end of town. Nobody else saw it, the ground was dry by the time anyone looked, and the matter has been referred to the weather office.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Mystery Hum Traced To Refrigerator At The Feed Store","body":"The low hum that has puzzled the east side for a month has been traced to a refrigerator at the feed store. It has been switched off and the mystery is over, to general disappointment.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Heat Wave Enters Third Week; Sidewalks Fry Eggs, Reporters Confirm","body":"Temperatures held above anything reasonable for a third week. The Dispatch tested the sidewalk-egg theory and can report that it works, if you like your eggs with grit.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Lizard Races Return To The Fairgrounds","body":"The annual lizard races drew a full grandstand this year. The favorite refused to leave the starting line, which is understandable in this heat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"October 2135","year":2135.0,"month":10.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"tourism_event_announced","headline":"Mark The Calendar: City Convention Comes In November 2135","body":"Old Bottle has announced City Convention for November 2135. Eligible visitor markets receive a seasonal event boost, subject to available transport, staff, beds, power and water.\n\nOrganizers warned that the event will be cancelled if its qualifying services are lost before the big day. Hotel managers were already counting rooms.","priority":500.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Barbershop Quartet Now A Trio; Tenor Moved To The Coast","body":"The town quartet has lost its tenor to a job on the coast. Auditions are open. Applicants are warned that the repertoire is mostly about trains.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Windmill Squeak Finally Oiled; Town Can't Sleep Without It","body":"The windmill by the stockyard has been oiled after years of squeaking. Several residents report insomnia and have asked for it to be put back the way it was.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Town Clock Repaired; Runs Fast Out Of Enthusiasm","body":"The courthouse clock has been repaired and now gains a minute a day. The clockmaker says it will settle down once it gets used to the heat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Well-Digging Contest Ends In Draw, Mud","body":"The well-digging contest at the fair ended when both teams struck water at the same moment and then each other. No winner was declared, but everyone was clean for once.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Mystery Hum Traced To Refrigerator At The Feed Store","body":"The low hum that has puzzled the east side for a month has been traced to a refrigerator at the feed store. It has been switched off and the mystery is over, to general disappointment.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"November 2135","year":2135.0,"month":11.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"Tumbleweeds Reclaim A Block Of Old Bottle","body":"Another 11 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Retired Prospector Finds Nothing, Reports Good Day","body":"A retired prospector returned from the hills with an empty sack and a broad smile. Asked what he found, he said quiet, and recommended it.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Sunset Declared Best Of The Year By Committee","body":"The sunset committee met on the ridge on Friday and declared this year's best. Minutes record it as orange with purple, which narrows it down somewhat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Petrified Log Returned To Roadside Attraction After Forty Years","body":"A petrified log taken from the roadside attraction decades ago arrived by post with an apology. The attraction has put it back and framed the letter.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Well-Digging Contest Ends In Draw, Mud","body":"The well-digging contest at the fair ended when both teams struck water at the same moment and then each other. No winner was declared, but everyone was clean for once.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Heat Wave Enters Third Week; Sidewalks Fry Eggs, Reporters Confirm","body":"Temperatures held above anything reasonable for a third week. The Dispatch tested the sidewalk-egg theory and can report that it works, if you like your eggs with grit.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]},{"title":"The Desert Dispatch","date":"December 2135","year":2135.0,"month":12.0,"day":22.0,"extra":false,"stories":[{"kind":"abandonment_wave","headline":"For-Sale Signs Bleach In The Sun At Old Bottle","body":"Another 22 buildings around Old Bottle were left empty this month. Owners cite a mix of taxes, traffic, crime and the general feeling that the grass is greener anywhere with grass.\n\nThe council was asked what it intends to do. Mayor Sierra said the matter was under review, which is what mayors say.","priority":360.0,"filler":false},{"kind":"","headline":"Neon Sign Repaired; Now Reads Correctly For First Time In Years","body":"The motel sign that has read MOT L since anyone can remember has been fixed. Longtime residents say it looks wrong.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Scorpion Found In Boot; Boot Found In Yard","body":"A resident discovered a scorpion in his boot on Monday morning. The boot was last seen traveling at speed across the lawn. Both are recovering.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Town Clock Repaired; Runs Fast Out Of Enthusiasm","body":"The courthouse clock has been repaired and now gains a minute a day. The clockmaker says it will settle down once it gets used to the heat.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Old-Timers Bench Gets New Slat; Old-Timers Suspicious","body":"The bench outside the courthouse has a new slat. Its regular occupants tested it for an afternoon and concluded that it will do, for now.","priority":0.0,"filler":true},{"kind":"","headline":"Snow Falls On Old Bottle; Nobody Owns A Shovel","body":"A rare snowfall dusted Old Bottle overnight and was gone by lunch. In the interval, residents photographed it, tasted it, and looked for a shovel that does not exist.","priority":0.0,"filler":true}]}]},"systems":{"power":{"shortage":false,"consumed":5098},"water":{"shortage":false,"consumed":6232,"treatment_adequate":false,"requested_demand":6258,"visitor_demand":382},"tourism":{"schema":3,"features":{"safety":{"period_month":2831,"active":true,"cost_half_cents":21590,"remainders":[{"instance":63,"micro":44000,"cursor":8,"opening_micro":792000,"opening_cursor":7,"month":2832},{"instance":66,"micro":564000,"cursor":7,"opening_micro":348000,"opening_cursor":7,"month":2832},{"instance":97,"micro":628000,"cursor":15,"opening_micro":342000,"opening_cursor":13,"month":2832},{"instance":92,"micro":50300,"cursor":6,"opening_micro":850700,"opening_cursor":3,"month":2832},{"instance":83,"micro":954600,"cursor":2,"opening_micro":814400,"opening_cursor":27,"month":2832},{"instance":82,"micro":828850,"cursor":18,"opening_micro":863250,"opening_cursor":16,"month":2832},{"instance":69,"micro":308550,"cursor":21,"opening_micro":153450,"opening_cursor":18,"month":2832},{"instance":87,"micro":432000,"cursor":15,"opening_micro":712000,"opening_cursor":14,"month":2832},{"instance":86,"micro":662000,"cur